@startuml
title "Unique shutdown order — 4 milestones per protocol (spec §3.4)"
start

:QUIESCING entered\n(gate stays OPEN);

fork
  :gRPC: migration_started\n(initiateServerDrain() -> Server.shutdown()\ntriggers built-in double GOAWAY, non-blocking);
fork again
  :Remoting: migration_started\n(GO_AWAY per clientVersion x invocation mode,\nor close idle channel);
end fork

note right
  Gate remains OPEN across the whole
  migration phase. Neither protocol
  waits for the other to start.
end note

fork
  :gRPC: wait for no_new_work_reached\npredicate from Step-1 spike\n(double GOAWAY itself, or bounded\nquiet window if new streams still possible);
fork again
  :Remoting: wait for no_new_work_reached\n(freezeRequestIntake() barrier crossed);
end fork

:last protocol to reach\nno_new_work_reached triggers\nadmission_closed\n(SendDrainGate.closeAdmission(), exactly once, global);

fork
  :gRPC: wait accepted_inflight_zero\n(grpcOpenSendRpcs == 0);
fork again
  :Remoting: wait accepted_inflight_zero\n(remotingPendingWrites == 0);
end fork

if (all terminals reached before\neffective deadline?) then (yes)
  :DRAINED;
else (no)
  :FORCE_DRAINING\n(forced close, drain marked failed);
endif

stop
@enduml

@startuml
title "Single clock budget timeline (spec §3.6)"
start
:T0 = beginDrain()\nenter QUIESCING, readiness fails,\nEndpointSlice / NLB detach starts;
:+60s -> lbCutoff\nreject any new business transport\nas late from here on;
:+420s (60+330+30) -> migrationCutoff\nclose admission if not already closed,\nfreeze intake;
:+450s -> drainHardDeadline\nmust reach DRAINED by here or force;
:+480s -> preStopWait\nPreStop / HTTP drain waiter absolute cap;
:+540s -> podGrace\nterminationGracePeriodSeconds;
:>=600s -> rollout step budget\n(next Pod replacement not started before this);
stop

note right
  Named budgets (must share one config source):
  D_provider_keep >= D_app_hard + D_skew + D_safety
  D_dependency_wait + D_app_hard + D_skew + D_safety <= D_provider_keep
  terminationGracePeriodSeconds >= D_prestop + D_process_stop + D_safety

  All of these are DERIVED from one config source,
  never re-defaulted independently in Helm / app / PreStop / supervisor.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title "Remoting beforeEnqueue admission decision (spec §9.4)"
start
:processor lookup;
if (already in global shutdown?) then (yes)
  :return existing\nversioned GO_AWAY behavior;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:classify request\n(producer send code? clientVersion? invocation mode);

if (lease not expired\nAND gate OPEN?) then (yes)
  :accepted\n(bind RemotingSendLifecycle(permit));
else (no)
  if (lease expired AND\nclientVersion > V5_3_1 AND\nnot oneway?) then (yes)
    :write GO_AWAY\n(do not dispatch to Broker);
  else (no)
    if (DRAINING or past lbCutoff\nAND clientVersion > V5_3_1?) then (yes)
      :write GO_AWAY\n(do not dispatch);
    else (no)
      if (legacy client past cutoff?) then (yes)
        :write SYSTEM_BUSY\n"[PROXY_DRAINING] retry another proxy"\nclose channel, count as degraded;
      else (no)
        if (channel closed before dispatch?) then (yes)
          :tryBackendSkipped(CHANNEL_CLOSED_BEFORE_DISPATCH)\n+ protocol terminal;
        else (no)
          :flow-control reject\n(rejectRequest / submit reject)\n-> synthetic backend terminal;
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
endif

if (accepted?) then (yes)
  :construct RequestTask\nwith RequestTaskContext;
  :submit to executor;
  if (submit rejected?) then (yes)
    :task skipped,\ntracked SYSTEM_BUSY response;
  else (no)
    :execute -> Broker dispatch;
  endif
endif
stop
@enduml

@startuml
title "gRPC send admission decision (spec §9.2)"
start
:ServerStreamTracer.newServerStreamTracer\ncreates GrpcSendLifecycleHolder,\nincrements grpcOpenSendRpcs;
:tracer.filterContext()\ninjects holder into io.grpc.Context;
:GrpcSendLifecycleInterceptor.interceptCall\nreads holder from Context;

if (non-send method?) then (yes)
  :next.startCall() directly\n(no gate interaction);
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (transport marked late\n(after lbCutoff) OR\ngate already CLOSED?) then (yes)
  :holder.tryBackendSkipped(...);
  :close call with\nStatus.UNAVAILABLE;
  stop
else (no)
endif

:gate.tryAcquire();
if (permit acquired?) then (yes)
  :CAS-bind permit to holder;
  :next.startCall() -> handler\n-> Broker dispatch;
  :Future completes ->\nbackendTerminal();
else (no, gate closed\nconcurrently)
  :holder.tryBackendSkipped(...);
  :close call with\nStatus.UNAVAILABLE;
endif

:streamClosed() is the only\ncanonical protocol terminal\n(decrements grpcOpenSendRpcs);
stop

note right
  Duplicate bind attempts, missing
  holder, or method mismatch must
  fail loudly (Status.INTERNAL) —
  never silently drop the permit.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title "Readiness — /ready vs /ready-for-traffic (spec §8.4)"
start
:STARTING;
:ReadinessBarrier evaluates\nall required contributors\n(listeners, MessagingProcessor,\nACL/TLS, NameServer sync,\nwarmup topics if configured);

if (all required succeed?) then (yes)
  :first transition\nSTARTING -> READY;
else (no)
  :stay NotReady,\nbackoff + retry\nuntil proxyWarmupTimeoutSeconds;
  stop
endif

repeat
  :contributor check tick;
  if (failureScope == LOCAL_FATAL?) then (yes)
    :/ready -> 503\n/ready-for-traffic -> 503\n(immediate fail-close, both endpoints);
  else (SHARED_DEPENDENCY)
    if (consecutive failures\n>= dependencyFailureThreshold?) then (yes)
      :/ready -> still 200 (fail-open)\n/ready-for-traffic -> 503 (fail-close);
    else (no)
      :/ready -> 200\n/ready-for-traffic -> 200\n(dependency still within tolerance);
    endif
  endif

  if (lifecycle state >= QUIESCING?) then (yes)
    :/ready -> 503, never recovers\neven if contributors succeed again;
    if (readyForTrafficDuringDrain == true\nAND provider spike proved safe?) then (yes)
      :/ready-for-traffic may stay 200\nuntil admission actually closes;
    else (no)
      :/ready-for-traffic -> 503\n(conservative default);
    endif
  endif
repeat while (not STOPPED)

:STOPPED -> both endpoints 503;
stop
@enduml

@startuml
title "Coordinator DRAINING fan-out / fan-in (spec §8.3)"
start
:T0: enter QUIESCING\n(readiness fails, both adapters\nnotified, gate stays OPEN);
:lbCutoff: enter MIGRATING\n(reject/count late transport,\nkeep waiting on existing leases);

if (business transport count == 0\nbefore migrationCutoff?) then (yes)
  :enter DRAINING early;
else (no)
  :migrationCutoff reached ->\nforce enter DRAINING;
endif

fork
  :gRPC adapter:\nstopAcceptingNewRpcs()\n-> GrpcServer.initiateServerDrain();
fork again
  :Remoting adapter:\nfreezeRequestIntake();
end fork

fork
  :gRPC: reach no_new_work_reached;
fork again
  :Remoting: reach no_new_work_reached;
end fork

:last-arriving protocol triggers\nsendDrainGate.closeAdmission()\n(single shared call);

fork
  :gRPC: await grpcOpenSendRpcs == 0;
fork again
  :Remoting: await remotingPendingWrites == 0;
end fork

:accepted_inflight_zero reached;

:closeAll(GrpcDrainStatusPolicy)\non non-send streaming calls\n(Telemetry -> OK, others -> UNAVAILABLE);
:close Remoting business channels;

fork
  :awaitServerTermination(effectiveDeadline);
fork again
  :await grpcOpenDrainableCalls == 0\nand Remoting ChannelGroup empty;
end fork

if (all conditions met before\neffective deadline?) then (yes)
  :DRAINED;
else (no)
  :FORCE_DRAINING\n(force-close both protocols,\nmark this drain forced);
endif
stop
@enduml

@startuml
title "Rollout / rollback flow (spec §6)"
start
:Canary release,\nlifecycle enabled,\nreal 5.0.7 / 5.2.1 / 5.3.2 clients,\nreal provider 8082 health check,\nsingle Pod delete verified;

:Pre-scale main cluster\n(capacity inequality, not a magic\nreplica count) + confirm no live HPA;

:One annotation-driven\nbootstrap rollout\n(binary + enableProxyAdminServer=true,\ncompressed into a single lossy rollout);

:Verify 8082 reachable\non every existing target;

if (all targets healthy on 8082?) then (yes)
  :Explicitly enable lifecycle=true\nin production values,\nswitch HTTP probes / PreStop /\nderived budgets / NLB health check;
else (no)
  :Stop — do not proceed\nto strict enablement;
  stop
endif

:Wait at least one full\nmax-lease + grace cycle;

if (forced / timeout / late-connection\nmetrics show zero increase?) then (yes)
  :Enable strict SLO,\nresume normal controlled rollout;
else (no)
  :Pause rollout,\nkeep existing READY Pods,\ninvestigate before retry;
endif
stop

note right
  On any send-SLO, connection-storm, or
  provider-detach anomaly during rollout:
  pause immediately, keep READY Pods,
  roll back only to a Helm revision that
  is binary+probe+PreStop compatible.
  Never auto-rollback.
end note
@enduml
